How Father Spent Sunday. THE new parson was making pastoral calls in his parish and stopped to converse with a small boy at the garden sate. "And where does your father go on Sundays, my little man?" "Well, on fine Sundays he goes golfing and on wet Sundays he turns us all out to church so he can have a bit of peace in the house." A MYSTERY SOLVED WITH E'S.
